Repository: pydantic/pydantic
Issue: #3295
Title: Empty objects should be validated as None for optional fields

Using `pydantic 2.7.1`, I wasn't able to find pydantic.annotated_arguments import

So here is another solution using [field_validator](https://docs.pydantic.dev/latest/concepts/validators/#field-validators)
```python
#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Python imports
from typing import Optional
# Packages imports
from pydantic import BaseModel, field_validator

class B(BaseModel):
    var3: str
    var4: str

class A(BaseModel):
    var1: int
    var2: Optional[B] = None

    @field_validator('var2', mode='before')
    def check_empty(cls, value):
        return value or None

if __name__ == "__main__":
    data = {
        "var1": 1,
        "var2": {}
    }
    result = A.model_validate(data)
    print(result)
```

